As far as I know, this must have been an earlier version of NetHack
than 3.1.3. In version 3.1.3, the lowest intrinsic AC you can get is
-10 (compared to your starting AC of +10).

Spoilers (sources)...

} else if (offer < (u.ulevel * 600) && u.ublessed < 20 &&
          (u.ublessed < 9 || !rn2(u.ublessed)))
          { verbalize("Thy devotion has been rewarded.");
            if (!(Protection & INTRINSIC))
               { Protection |= FROMOUTSIDE;
                 if (!u.ublessed)  u.ublessed = rn1(3, 2);
               } else u.ublessed++;
          }

What this means:

First, your offer must be greater than or equal to 400 times, and less
than 600 times your level in gold (the "400" is somewhere earlier in
the code). Then, your intrinsic armour class (IAC, the u.ublessed
variable) must be less than 20. Then, your IAC must be either less than
9 or you only have a 1-in-(current IAC) chance that your IAC will be
improved. If these conditions have been fullfilled, your IAC will be
increased.

The first time you get a blessing, you get the "Protection" intrinsic,
and your IAC is increased by 2-5 points. Any subsequent increases are
only 1.

Again, please note that your IAC MUST BE smaller than 20 for the
blessing to take effect. If your intrinsic AC is already at -10 (as
compared to your starting +10 AC), you won't get any more AC benefits
from donating money to a priest.

